   "fix": "Add `antilinearOfOneL_apply_I_smul : antilinearOfOneL V v (Complex.I \u2022 w) = -(Complex.I \u2022 antilinearOfOneL V v w)`, stated in the same form as the `hL` hypothesis of `antilinearOfOneL_apply_one`. Optionally also add `@[simp] antilinearOfOneL_apply_apply_one : antilinearOfOneL V v 1 = v`, which makes `v \u21a6 antilinearOfOneL V v` and `L \u21a6 L 1` mutual inverses on antilinear maps.",
   "issue": "`antilinearOfOneL` lacks its defining property: nothing proves `antilinearOfOneL V v` is complex antilinear, so a consumer has to unfold to `re \u2b1d v - im \u2b1d (I \u2022 v)` before using it as an antilinear map. Only `antilinearOfOneL_apply` (unfolding) and `antilinearOfOneL_apply_one` (antilinear `L` equals `antilinearOfOneL (L 1)`) are provided.",
